<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#zasagt-khan">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zasagt Khan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zasagt Khan was the title of the Chinggisid rulers of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha Mongols</a>, one of the three, later four, Khalkha khanates. The title was adopted in the late 16th century by a branch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geresenje">Geresenje</a>'s descendants ruling towards the Khangai and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altai-mountains">Altai</a> mountains. After the Khalkha submitted to the Qing in 1691, the Zasagt Khan became a Qing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> prince.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zasagt-khan.jpg" alt="Zasagt Khan" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 瑞丽江的河水 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%89%8E%E8%90%A8%E5%85%8B%E5%9B%BE%E6%B1%97%E9%83%A8%E4%BD%8D%E7%BD%AE%E5%9B%BE1820.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
